  "id": "ea4c33e7-98cb-4f2d-b23e-cd55d255d9ac",
  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $k$ be a positive integer and $f(x)=e^x-1$. Then\n\\[\n\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{f(x)+f(x/2)+f(x/2^2)+\\cdots+f(x/2^k)}{x}\n\\]\nis",
  "options": {
    "A": "$2-\\frac1{2^k}$",
    "B": "$2-\\frac1{2^{k+1}}$",
    "C": "$k$",
    "D": "$2^{k+1}-1$"
  },
  "answer": "A",
  "solution": "Using $\\lim_{x\\to0}(e^x-1)/x=1$ termwise, the limit is\n\\[\n1+\\frac12+\\frac1{2^2}+\\cdots+\\frac1{2^k}=2-\\frac1{2^k}.\n\\]\n",
